hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"501","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The world is cursed, and cursed is what is in it, except what is for Allah of it."
"502","al-Hasan ibn Shawkar narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ja'far narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz, meaning al-Majishun, from Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, from Ibrahim ibn Murrah, who said: A scorpion stung the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: What is with it, may Allah curse it; it cares neither for a prophet nor for anyone else."
"503","Muhammad ibn al-Musaffa narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated to us, from al-Wadin ibn Ata, from Yazid ibn Marthad al-Mudda'i, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The spider is a devil, so kill it."
